    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Note for \"Supabase - Update Status\" node\n1. Just update the backtest_status in track_requests Table. The final ticker_status will be updated by the DB at the DB level. - done\n2. add a gate checker after merge results, where only after workflow receives both  signals from save results, then the ticker status backtest status flag to complete. --DONE\n3. add another trigger at the end which then automatically triggers the ai analysis workflow. \n4. add a flag for ffm analysis like backtest results : pending, processing, complete. \npending is automatic when initiated. -- DONE",
        "height": 304,
        "width": 592
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1168,
        1328
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "afc0b642-e4b3-441f-8345-53f17760888a",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"message\": \"Analysis started\",\n  \"request_id\": \"{{ $json.body.request_id }}\",\n  \"check_status_at\": \"http://63.179.141.203:8002/api/v1/status/{{ $json.body.request_id }}\"\n}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.4,
      "position": [
        -304,
        544
      ],
      "id": "3306f30b-3630-4d2f-aa52-99133cae7293",
      "name": "Respond to Webhook1"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const requestId = $input.first().json.request_id;\nconst maxAttempts = 15;  // 15 × 3 = 45 seconds (safe margin)\nconst waitTime = 3000;\n\nfor (let i = 0; i < maxAttempts; i++) {\n  const options = {\n    method: 'GET',\n    url: `http://63.179.141.203:8002/api/v1/status/${requestId}`,\n    headers: {\n      'Content-Type': 'application/json'\n    },\n    json: true\n  };\n  \n  const status = await this.helpers.httpRequest(options);\n  \n  // Check if both complete\n  if (status.statuses && \n      status.statuses.ffm_status === 'complete' && \n      status.statuses.backtest_status === 'complete') {\n    return [{ \n      json: { \n        ...status, \n        request_id: requestId,\n        attempts: i + 1,\n        time_elapsed: (i + 1) * 3\n      } \n    }];\n  }\n  \n  // Check for failures\n  if (status.statuses && \n      (status.statuses.ffm_status === 'failed' || \n       status.statuses.backtest_status === 'failed')) {\n    throw new Error(`Analysis failed: ${status.statuses.error_log || 'Unknown error'}`);\n  }\n  \n  // Wait before next attempt\n  if (i < maxAttempts - 1) {\n    await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, waitTime));\n  }\n}\n\n// If we get here, analysis is still running but we're out of time\nthrow new Error('Analysis still running after 45 seconds. Try checking results manually at: http://63.179.141.203:8002/api/v1/status/' + requestId);"
      },
      "id": "208fd24d-909b-4620-b1de-8c3932e5e8c4",
      "name": "Poll Status Until Complete",
